{"timestamp":"2026-04-14T19:47:02.267Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"`backfillAttachCheckpointToV2` exists to handle one specific edge case: `attach` is adding a session to a checkpoint that already exists in v1, but v2 was not enabled when that checkpoint was originally created. In that situation, writing only the newly attached session to v2 would create a partial v2 copy of the checkpoint, and later v2-preferring reads could see incomplete data. The function avoids that by rebuilding the entire checkpoint in v2 from the authoritative v1 copy. See [attach.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:221).\n\nWhat it does:\n\n- It reads the v1 checkpoint summary with `v1Store.ReadCommitted(...)` to discover all sessions already in that checkpoint, not just the one being attached. [attach.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:224)\n- It loops over every session index in that summary and loads each full session payload from v1 with `ReadSessionContent(...)`. [attach.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:236)\n- For each session, it reuses the migration path helper `buildMigrateWriteOpts(...)` to reconstruct `WriteCommittedOptions` for v2 from the v1 metadata and transcript. That keeps attach aligned with the existing v1→v2 conversion logic instead of inventing a second mapping. [attach.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:245), [migrate.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:395)\n- If a compact transcript can be generated, it adds `CompactTranscript` plus the correct compact offset via `computeCompactOffset(...)`, so v2 `/main` gets `transcript.jsonl` and correct `checkpoint_transcript_start`. [attach.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:249), [migrate.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:470)\n- It writes each session into v2 with `v2Store.WriteCommitted(...)`. Because v2 deduplicates by `SessionID`, this reconstructs the checkpoint incrementally without duplicating already-known sessions. [attach.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:254)\n- If any session is a task checkpoint, it also copies task metadata trees into v2 `/full/current`, matching the existing migration behavior. [attach.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:259)\n\nSo the short version is: it is a targeted “repair/backfill” path for legacy v1-only checkpoints, used during attach, to ensure that once v2 is enabled the whole checkpoint appears in v2 consistently rather than only the newest attached session.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
