on into v2 with `v2Store.WriteCommitted(...)`. Because v2 deduplicates by `SessionID`, this reconstructs the checkpoint incrementally without duplicating already-known sessions. [attach.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:254)\n- If any session is a task checkpoint, it also copies task metadata trees into v2 `/full/current`, matching the existing migration behavior. [attach.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:259)\n\nSo the short version is: it is a targeted “repair/backfill” path for legacy v1-only checkpoints, used during attach, to ensure that once v2 is enabled the whole checkpoint appears in v2 consistently rather than only the newest attached session."}],"phase":"final_answer"}}
