sion appended\n- naive v2 dual-write would create only the new session under:\n  - `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main:<cp-path>/0/transcript.jsonl`\n  - `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/current:<cp-path>/0/raw_transcript`\n- the older v1-only sessions would still be absent from v2\n\n**Minimal repo-level example**\n\n1. `entire` enabled, but no `checkpoints_v2`\n2. attach `session-1` on `HEAD`\n3. commit now points to checkpoint `X` in v1 only\n4. set `.entire/settings.json` to `{\"enabled\": true, \"strategy_options\": {\"checkpoints_v2\": true}}`\n5. attach `session-2` on the same `HEAD`\n6. without backfill:\n   - v1 checkpoint `X` contains `session-1` + `session-2`\n   - v2 checkpoint `X` contains only `session-2`\n\nThat exact scenario is what [TestAttach_V2BackfillsExistingV1OnlyCheckpoint](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/attach_test.go:228) covers.\n\nSo `entire migrate` could fix it later, but without `backfillAttachCheckpointToV2`, `attach` itself could create an inconsistent v2 checkpoint immediately.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
