{"timestamp":"2026-04-14T19:52:11.758Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","turn_id":"019d8d8c-d0e3-70c2-8bd0-cbd5c2a725c5","last_agent_message":"Because the checkpoint can already belong to a different session.\n\nThe session being attached is not the reason the checkpoint exists. The checkpoint may already be on `HEAD` from an earlier session, and `attach` is adding another session into that same checkpoint.\n\nThe concrete case is:\n\n1. Session `A` was already captured earlier.\n   This could have happened via normal hooks, or via an earlier `entire attach`.\n2. That created checkpoint `X` and put `Entire-Checkpoint: X` on the current commit.\n3. At that time, `checkpoints_v2` was off, so `X` exists only in v1.\n4. Later, a separate session `B` happens against the same commit, but hooks don’t capture it, so `B` is unattached.\n5. Now you enable `checkpoints_v2`.\n6. You run `entire attach <session-B>`.\n7. `attach` sees that `HEAD` already has checkpoint `X`, so it reuses `X` instead of creating a new checkpoint. That behavior is in [attach.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:284).\n\nSo without backfill, v2 would get only session `B`, while v1 already had session `A` and now also `B`.\n\nThat is the inconsistency:\n\n- v1 checkpoint `X` = `A + B`\n- v2 checkpoint `X` = `B` only\n\nSo the issue is not “why would the checkpoint exist before the session is attached?”  \nIt exists because it came from an earlier session on the same commit.\n\nA realistic example:\n\n1. You make a code change with Claude and commit it. Hooks work. Checkpoint `X` is created.\n2. Later you do a research/debug session on the same commit, but hooks were missing or broken.\n3. You run `entire attach` for that research session.\n4. `attach` adds that research session into existing checkpoint `X`, not a new checkpoint.\n\nThat exact scenario is what [TestAttach_V2BackfillsExistingV1OnlyCheckpoint](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/attach_test.go:228) is modeling.","completed_at":1776196331,"duration_ms":22537}}
